        "description": "Retrieves case facts and precedents to build a task-specific prompt for legal LLM analysis.\n\nThis node prepares a structured prompt for a legal LLM by querying two vector databases: one for the current/new case and another for historic precedents. It first normalizes the user’s selected task (summary, verdict, progress, precedents, or arguments for either party) and expands the query with domain‑specific keywords to improve retrieval quality. The node then fetches the top‑relevant chunks from both databases, combines them with a strict instruction set (including mandatory rules about grounding every conclusion in the provided context), and outputs a single prompt string ready for an LLM. This design ensures that the LLM’s analysis is confined to authoritative case materials and follows legal reasoning conventions.",
