    {
      "id": "gt1zrykmw",
      "node_id": "node-context-generator-(llama)-0eb353fd",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Text Generate (Llama)",
      "description": {
        "text": "This node performs autoregressive text generation using a preloaded LLaMA-based language model, producing a continuation or response from a given prompt. The model and tokenizer are already loaded by the wrapper, so the node focuses on input preparation and controlled generation.\n\nThe prompt is first tokenized and moved to the same device as the model (typically GPU). The node then invokes the model’s generate function with configurable parameters such as max_new_tokens (output length), temperature (controls randomness), top_p (nucleus sampling), and do_sample (enables probabilistic generation). The pad_token_id is set to ensure proper sequence termination.\n\nAfter generation, the output tokens are decoded into readable text with special tokens removed. The final result is a clean string representing the model’s generated continuation, suitable for chat, completion, or downstream processing.",
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-context-generator-(llama)-0eb353fd",
        "name": "Text Generate (Llama)",
        "description": "This node performs autoregressive text generation using a preloaded LLaMA-based language model, producing a continuation or response from a given prompt. The model and tokenizer are already loaded by the wrapper, so the node focuses on input preparation and controlled generation.\n\nThe prompt is first tokenized and moved to the same device as the model (typically GPU). The node then invokes the model’s generate function with configurable parameters such as max_new_tokens (output length), temperature (controls randomness), top_p (nucleus sampling), and do_sample (enables probabilistic generation). The pad_token_id is set to ensure proper sequence termination.\n\nAfter generation, the output tokens are decoded into readable text with special tokens removed. The final result is a clean string representing the model’s generated continuation, suitable for chat, completion, or downstream processing.",
